# Test: ze show host thermal runs offline and emits a JSON object without a daemon
# VALIDATES: offline fallback -- `show host thermal` runs the in-process
#            host.DetectThermal when no daemon is reachable, marshaling the
#            ThermalInfo (hwmon sensors + per-core throttle counters) to a
#            JSON object and exiting 0.
# PREVENTS: regressions where show host thermal silently requires a daemon,
#           errors out, or emits non-JSON.
# PLATFORM: host inventory scans /sys/class/hwmon + thermal_throttle; the
# darwin detector (thermal_other.go) returns ErrUnsupported at build time.
# Skip on darwin per rules/os-specific-tests.md.
# LIMITATION: ThermalInfo.Sensors and .Throttle are both `omitempty`, so a
# host with no hwmon sensors and no thermal_throttle counters (the QEMU CI
# host) emits the empty object `{}`. No per-section field can be asserted
# non-vacuously here without thermal hardware, so this test asserts the
# offline JSON-object contract only; DetectThermal dispatch within the full
# inventory is additionally covered by cli-host-all-show.ci.
option=skip-os:value=darwin
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp { }
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze show host thermal
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains={
